## Rule of the Court (DIFC RDC Part 38)
##
## Source: Rules of the DIFC Courts, Part 38 (Costs).
## Specifically encoded here: assessed costs on a standard basis comprise
## reasonable and proportionate professional time plus disbursements
## (including the court filing fee).
##
## This file expresses the rule applied in:
##   CFI 058/2024 — Atul Dhawan Ashok Amir Chand Dhawan v Ramzi Wahib El Jaouhari
##   Order with Reasons of H.E. Justice Roger Stewart KC, 31 March 2026.
## Where the court awarded costs "as claimed" — i.e. the formula below
## evaluated against the schedule of costs produced the same total the
## court ordered.

```catala
declaration structure CostsClaim:
  data hours_worked content decimal
  data hourly_rate_aed content decimal
  data court_fee_aed content decimal

declaration structure CostsAward:
  data professional_time_aed content decimal
  data disbursements_aed content decimal
  data total_aed content decimal

declaration scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  input claim content CostsClaim
  output award content CostsAward

scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  definition award equals
    let pt equals claim.hours_worked * claim.hourly_rate_aed in
    let db equals claim.court_fee_aed in
    CostsAward {
      -- professional_time_aed: pt;
      -- disbursements_aed: db;
      -- total_aed: pt + db
    }
```

## Test — facts of CFI 058/2024

```catala
declaration scope TestDhawan:
  output assessment content StandardBasisAssessment

scope TestDhawan:
  definition assessment equals
    StandardBasisAssessment of {
      -- claim:
        CostsClaim {
          -- hours_worked: 3.0;
          -- hourly_rate_aed: 2000.0;
          -- court_fee_aed: 1121.75
        }
    }

  assertion assessment.award.total_aed = 7121.75
```
